      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eafb465a-21b8-5658-9048-8cfadaf031db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leslie Skinner\n- Products: Bazooka\n- Systems: shoulder-fired missiles, MANPADS, MPADS, shoulder-launched surface-to-air missiles\n- Topics: rocket-propelled weapons, anti-tank weapons, infantry combat\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, Leslie Skinner played a leading role in developing several rocket-propelled weapons, notably the Bazooka.\n- The Bazooka was the first shoulder-fired missile system.\n- The Bazooka was also referred to as the \"Stovepipe.\"\n- The Bazooka was among the first generation of rocket-propelled anti-tank weapons used in infantry combat.\n- Bazooka is often used informally as a name for shoulder-fired missiles, although the actual Bazooka is a distinct original type of shoulder-fired missile.\n- Man-portable air-defense systems, abbreviated MANPADS or MPADS, are shoulder-launched surface-to-air missiles.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7a35e4ca-519f-54d8-aa1f-97305faba02f",
        "text": "Page: Leslie Skinner. Sentence: He played a leading role in the development of several rocket propelled weapons during World War II, notably the first shoulder-fired missile system, the Bazooka.\nPage: Bazooka. Sentence: Also referred to as the \"Stovepipe\", the innovative bazooka was among the first generation of rocket-propelled anti-tank weapons used in infantry combat.\nPage: Shoulder-fired missile. Sentence: In many instances, although not technically defining all shoulder-fired missiles, the name Bazooka is used as an informal name regularly, although the actual Bazooka is a type of original shoulder-fired missile in its own right.\nPage: Man-portable air-defense system. Sentence: Man-portable air-defense systems (MANPADS or MPADS) are shoulder-launched surface-to-air missiles (SLSAMs).",
